  "title": "Chapter 25: State Government Structure",
  "order": 26,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i3djheo",
      "content": "The Constitution of India provides a federal system with powers divided between the Union and the States. The structure of the State Government is similar to that of the Central Government. It consists of the Governor, Chief Minister, Council of Ministers, and the State Legislature. The provisions related to State Government are mainly found in Part VI of the Constitution (Articles 153–237)."
    },
